          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भक्तिः — bhaktiḥ — \"devotion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जनाः भक्त्या नदीं नमन्ति। janāḥ bhaktyā nadīṃ namanti. People bow to the river with devotion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भक्तिः (bhaktiḥ) comes from the root √bhaj, \"to share, worship\", as in bhajati; MW gives bhakti as a share, and also attachment, devotion, worship, faith (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
